  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Myanmar Acute Joint Response 2025</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The humanitarian situation in Myanmar has worsened significantly following the devastating earthquake in March 2025. Widespread damage to infrastructure, buildings, and roads has caused critical shortages of essential supplies and worsened the already dire living conditions. Sagaing and Mandalay states are among the hardest-hit regions, experiencing severe destruction and mass displacement, with 4.8 million people in urgent need of aid even before the earthquake. 

TF/KBC/CPM will provide MPC and Protection support to address the urgent needs of 1,000 most affected HHs (5,000 people) in Shwe Bo Township in Sagaing state and Aung Myay Thar Zan and Pyi Gyi Tagon (East) Townships in Mandalay state.</narrative>
  </description>
